# CLAUDE.md (sanitized excerpt)

Infrastructure repo for two Proxmox hosts and their guests. The agent runs in its own unprivileged container as a
normal user with no sudo. Machine names, addresses and logins live in `servers.md`.

## Golden rules

- **Pull first.** The hosts push their live config to this repo every hour, so run `git pull --rebase` before
  editing anything. If a pull brings changes to files you deployed, redeploy the merged versions.
- **The repo mirrors live files.** `hosts/<machine>/<path>` is the live `/<path>` on that machine. Live wins: the next
  sync overwrites repo edits that weren't deployed. Deploy with the `/deploy` skill.
- **Never deploy redacted files** (configs whose secrets are stripped before they reach git).
- **Back up before overwriting live files** (`/root/bak-before-<change>.tgz` on the target), and verify afterwards.
- **Root steps the permission mode blocks: don't retry them.** Give the person one copyable block of commands for the
  host shell, then check the result read-only.
- **Secrets never go in git.** Security changes are logged in a file outside the repo.

## Checks before deploying

- Python: the lint hook runs after every edit; run a full `ruff check <files>` before deploying anyway.
- Shell: `shellcheck`. JS: `node --check`.
- Browser checks: read-only checks may hit the live site. Anything that clicks or saves runs against a scratch copy
  of the app with a copy of its database.

## Defaults the person wants

- Dark theme and 24-hour clocks everywhere. One time zone on every machine; convert UTC times before saying them.
- Everything auto-updates. Reboots that need a person show up on the health page first, with a deadline.
- Anything that needs a person's attention shows up on the health page, nowhere else.
- Plans and to-dos are plain `.md` files in the notes folder (the `save-note` skill), not chat history.
- Commit and push when the work is done.
